I have traced the complete path. Here is the full POST /api/owners creation path, in call order.

## Endpoint binding

The HTTP mapping lives on the generated `OwnersApi` interface (from OpenAPI); the controller only overrides the method. `POST /api/owners` → `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`. The request body binds to `OwnerFieldsDto` and is validated with `@Valid` (declared on the generated interface method), and the controller registers an extra `Validator` via `@InitBinder`.

The generated interface is at `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java` (POST mapping to `/api/owners`, consumes `application/json`, `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`). There is also a V2 controller (`OwnerRestControllerV2`) but it only exposes a paged GET (`listOwnersPage`) — it does NOT handle creation.

---

## 1. Controller method

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

InitBinder that adds the custom validator (lines 127-130):
```java
@InitBinder("ownerFieldsDto")
void initOwnerFieldsBinder(WebDataBinder binder) {
    binder.addValidators(ownerFieldsValidator);
}
```

The creation handler (lines 157-184):
```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    owner.setAddress(addressNormalizer.normalize(owner.getAddress()));
    LocalDate registrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate() != null
        ? owner.getRegistrationDate() : LocalDate.now();
    owner.setRegistrationDate(businessDayAdjuster.toBusinessDay(registrationDate));
    String telephone = telephoneNormalizer.normalize(owner.getTelephone());
    if (!this.clinicService.findOwnerByTelephone(telephone).isEmpty()) {
        throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(telephone);
    }
    dailyRegistrationLimitValidator.validate(owner.getRegistrationDate());
    cityCapacityValidator.validate(owner);
    if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold())) {
        householdAssigner.assignSharedHousehold(owner);
    } else {
        householdDuplicateValidator.validate(owner);
    }
    owner.setTelephone(telephone);
    owner.setEmail(emailNormalizer.normalize(owner.getEmail()));
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

Note: `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` gates the endpoint (Spring Security). Returns `201 CREATED` with a `Location` header.

---

## The full ordered chain of validations and side-effects

Executing `addOwner` step by step:

1. Bean Validation (`@Valid`) + custom `OwnerFieldsValidator` run BEFORE the method body (on binding). Failures → `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400.
2. `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` — maps DTO to entity (id/pets/customerCode/householdId/namesakeCount ignored).
3. `addressNormalizer.normalize(...)` — canonicalizes address.
4. Registration date defaults to `LocalDate.now()` if absent, then `businessDayAdjuster.toBusinessDay(...)` rolls weekends to Monday.
5. `telephoneNormalizer.normalize(...)` — to E.164; invalid → `InvalidTelephoneException` → 400.
6. `clinicService.findOwnerByTelephone(...)` — duplicate phone → `DuplicateTelephoneException` → 409.
7. `dailyRegistrationLimitValidator.validate(...)` — >=100/day → `DailyRegistrationLimitExceededException` → 429.
8. `cityCapacityValidator.validate(owner)` — >=50/city → `CityCapacityExceededException` → 409.
9. Branch on `sharesHousehold`:
   - true → `householdAssigner.assignSharedHousehold(owner)` (may back-fill and SAVE existing household members — a side effect).
   - false/null → `householdDuplicateValidator.validate(owner)` — duplicate household → `DuplicateHouseholdException` → 409.
10. Set normalized telephone and normalized email onto entity.
11. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` — generates customerCode, computes namesakeCount, persists.
12. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` — builds response (derives displayName, initials, membershipNumber, membershipTier, locality).
13. Set `Location` header, return 201.

