Normalizers used before/within validation:
- `TelephoneNormalizer.normalize` (`.../rest/controller/TelephoneNormalizer.java`) — E.164; throws `InvalidTelephoneException` (default country code `61`, 8–15 digits).
- `AddressNormalizer.normalize` (`.../rest/controller/AddressNormalizer.java`) — trims/collapses/uppercases, expands ST/RD/AVE; null/blank → "".
- `EmailNormalizer.normalize` (`.../rest/controller/EmailNormalizer.java`) — trims/lowercases; blank → null.
- `BusinessDayAdjuster.toBusinessDay` (`.../rest/controller/BusinessDayAdjuster.java`) — weekend → next Monday.

`Households` (`.../rest/controller/Households.java`) — shared household-key logic used by the duplicate guard and the assigner. `findMembers` calls `clinicService.findOwnerByLastNameIgnoreCase` then filters by a normalized `lastName + "\n" + address` key. `stableId` derives a deterministic UUID from that key.

Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (interface, MapStruct) and generated impl `target/generated-sources/annotations/.../OwnerMapperImpl.java`. `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` copies firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone/email/registrationDate only. `toOwnerDto` computes derived read-only fields (displayName, initials, membershipNumber, membershipTier, locality).

